{{!
    @template enrol_apply/manage

    Decision form wrapping the table of pending enrolment applications.

    The table markup is produced by table_sql and passed in already rendered, so it is
    output with a triple stash. Everything else is escaped normally.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * formurl string - url the decision form posts back to
    * sesskey string - session key guarding the state change
    * capacityhtml string - the decision context above the table, already rendered. OUTSIDE the
      hasrows section for the same reason the two notices are: a method whose applicant limit is
      reached has an EMPTY queue, and its numbers are what explain that
    * tablehtml string - pre-rendered applications table
    * hasrows boolean - whether the table has at least one application
    * showingtext string - which rows of how many are on screen, shown only where there are rows
    * hasplacesnotice boolean - whether every place on the method is taken
    * placesnotice string - the sentence saying so
    * hasclosednotice boolean - whether the method has reached its applicant limit and is
      refusing new applications. Rendered outside the hasrows section on purpose: the state it
      names can legitimately hold an EMPTY queue, which is exactly when nothing else explains it
    * closednotice string - the sentence saying so, naming how many of the held applications are
      deferred, because a deferred row is freed by nothing and cancelling those is the way out
    * stickyfooter string - the bulk action bar, already rendered into a core sticky footer by
      the renderer and interpolated INSIDE this form, because the POST carries the row checkboxes
      from the table and the action from the bar. Core does the same in grade/templates/edit_tree
      and the sticky footer is never moved in the DOM - its placement is CSS, not JavaScript, so
      the inputs inside it post normally.
    * everything enrol_apply/decision_controls requires - the group chooser, the role chooser
      and the message box are that partial's, shared with the single-application review page so
      the two decision surfaces cannot drift. See it for what each variable means and for which
      spelling of a name each stash wants.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "formurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?id=7",
        "sesskey": "Ab12Cd34Ef",
        "hasplacesnotice": true,
        "placesnotice": "All 20 places on this enrolment method are taken.",
        "hasclosednotice": true,
        "closednotice": "This enrolment method holds 40 of a maximum 40 applications and is accepting no more. 12 of them are deferred; cancelling the ones no longer needed makes room.",
        "capacityhtml": "<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"card-body\">12 awaiting decision</div></div>",
        "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>Student 1</td></tr></tbody></table>",
        "hasrows": true,
        "showingtext": "Showing 1-4 of 4",
        "stickyfooter": "<div id=\"sticky-footer\"><button type=\"submit\">Go</button></div>",
        "messagelabel": "Message to the applicant",
        "messagehelp": "Included in the message they receive. Optional.",
        "messagevalue": "",
        "notelabel": "Note for the record",
        "notehelp": "Kept with the application for whoever looks at it next. The applicant never sees it.",
        "notevalue": "",
        "hasgroups": true,
        "grouplabel": "Groups to join on approval",
        "grouphelp": "Leave empty to use the groups configured on the enrolment method.",
        "groups": [
            {"id": 3, "name": "Tutorial A"},
            {"id": 4, "name": "R&D < Team"}
        ],
        "hasroles": true,
        "rolelabel": "Role to assign on approval",
        "rolehelp": "Leave it alone to use the role configured on the enrolment method.",
        "roledefault": "Use the enrolment method's role",
        "roles": [
            {"id": 5, "name": "Student"},
            {"id": 3, "name": "R&amp;D &lt; Team"}
        ]
    }
}}
<form id="enrol_apply_manage_form" class="enrol_apply-manage" method="post" action="{{formurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    {{#hasplacesnotice}}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">{{placesnotice}}</div>
    {{/hasplacesnotice}}
    {{#hasclosednotice}}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">{{closednotice}}</div>
    {{/hasclosednotice}}
    {{{capacityhtml}}}
    <div class="enrol_apply-table">
        {{{tablehtml}}}
    </div>
    {{#hasrows}}
        <div class="enrol_apply-showing small text-muted mb-3">{{showingtext}}</div>
        {{> enrol_apply/decision_controls }}
        {{{stickyfooter}}}
    {{/hasrows}}
</form>
